# Everything here is left out of the build context, which is the set of files
# sent to Docker before the build even starts.

# Installed inside the image instead, from the lock file. Copying these in
# would be 400MB of files built for the wrong operating system.
node_modules

# Build output from running npm run build on the laptop. The image builds its
# own, and an old one here would quietly end up in the image.
.next

# Real secrets. .env.example only has placeholders so it can stay.
.env*
!.env.example
